You can, you have to look up
what the components are for it.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:59.470
Maybe in your class you have to memorize
the different lipids, but hopefully not.

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:02.379
What you're gonna be doing is
there's two components, right?

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.090
So the first one is glycerol.

00:03:04.589 --> 00:03:09.830
What I would recommend doing is if you are
taking a biochemistry course is memorize

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.769
what the structure of glycerol looks like.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:17.120
Remember, there's going to be three
carbons connected to each other, and each

