00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:36.480
Now, notice with this structure,
we don't have enough acids.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.439
So it's going to take three of
them for this to happen, right?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.570
So all this is going to be occurring
under, um, just under, usually under

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:50.130
acidic conditions or usually or maybe
it's being heated when this is happening.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.239
So we will have our three
different components.

00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:56.989
So we're going to have three
of them lined up just like so.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.619
And what are we going to be removing?

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:04.595
is we're going to be removing
water as a result, right.

00:04:04.615 --> 00:04:10.285
So just like how we did before,
we're going to copy and paste

00:04:10.335 --> 00:04:14.215
those guys so that we can show
